## Problem

Breaking syntax/API changes in aztec.js and aztec.nr reach the docs unevenly. An analysis of the last 12 months of breaking commits (`feat!`/`refactor!`/etc. touching `yarn-project/aztec.js` or `noir-projects/**/aztec-nr`) found 51% add a migration note, only 33% touch any real doc example or prose, and 45% ship no docs change at all. CI protects `#include_code` snippets and `docs/examples/` (both compiled/typechecked), but nothing protects hand-written inline snippets and prose — and the `/release-docs` skill has no step that applies the release's breaking changes to the docs before the versioned snapshot is cut. Full write-up: https://gist.github.com/AztecBot/74ce3afdf643c0b74d0cb1b3de8cfce6

Three changes:

## 1. `/release-docs` Step 8b: sweep the release's syntax changes into the docs

New step between migration-note triage (Step 8) and the snapshot cut (Step 11):

- **Enumerate** breaking changes from `git diff v<old>..v<new> -- docs/.../migration_notes.md` (the only machine-extractable breaking-change signal in the repo — component tags + literal `**Migration:**` diff blocks), cross-checked against `git log --grep='!:'` over the tag range. Explicitly *not* the GitHub release body (hand-written prose, unreliable sectioning) and *not* the migration-notes `## <version>` headings (unreliable version attribution).
- **Locate** old-syntax usages by grep, prioritizing surfaces with no compiler gate (inline snippets, `aztec-nr/` prose, `docs-operate/`).
- **Adjudicate** every hit against the source at the tag before editing — a prototype run showed raw symbol greps are mostly false positives (symbols that survive with changed arguments, third-party SDK snippets, historical prose), so the step spells out dismissal rules.
- **Report** a `component | old → new | fixed | dismissed` table for user review.

Key Points updated to match.

## 2. Wire up the orphaned aztec.js single-page reference generator

`docs-developers/docs/aztec-js/aztec_js_reference.md` is auto-generated by `docs/scripts/aztecjs_reference_generation/`, but that generator was wired to nothing — no yarn script, no CI hook, no release-docs step — and the page had not been regenerated since 2025-12-10, across four releases.

- New `yarn generate:aztecjs-reference` script (`update_docs.sh current`); `typescript` added to docs devDependencies so the parser resolves without a monorepo build.
- `/release-docs` Step 6 now runs it (working tree is at the release tag there, so the page reflects what shipped); documented in `docs/README.md`.
- The stale page is regenerated in this PR. Regeneration surfaced a JSDoc typo (`meatadata`) and forbidden `on-chain` spellings in aztec.js source doc comments — fixed at the source (comment-only changes), plus `fastforward` added to the docs dictionary.

## 3. Fill `references:` frontmatter on 158 docs pages

`docs/scripts/check_doc_references.sh` detects when a PR changes source files that docs document (devrel review request + #docs-alerts ping + ClaudeBox dispatch) — but only 35 of 233 source docs pages declared `references:`, with a single aztec.js path among them, so the system was largely dormant.

- 158 pages across `docs-developers/`, `docs-operate/`, `docs-participate/`, and `docs/docs/` now declare verified `references:` (287 unique source paths; every path checked to exist; single-line array format required by the extractor).
- The extractor (`extract_doc_references.sh`) now also scans `.mdx` pages — the operator guided-setup pages are `.mdx` and were previously invisible to it.
- Pages with no meaningful in-repo source mapping were deliberately left without references rather than given invented ones: external-repo content (aztec-standards AIPs, DappNode, staking dashboard), historical changelogs, glossaries, and pure navigation/community pages.

## Validation

- All 287 referenced paths verified to exist from the repo root (CI extractor semantics, `/*` dir suffixes stripped).
- Each of the 158 pages is exactly a one-line frontmatter addition; format checked against the CI awk parser.
- `yarn spellcheck` over all 446 docs files: 0 issues (including the regenerated reference).
- `yarn preprocess` passes; `yarn generate:aztecjs-reference` run end-to-end to produce the committed page.

